@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Creating a Stored Procedure";
}

<div class="container-fluid py-4">

    <!-- =========================
         PAGE HEADER
    ========================== -->

    <div class="mb-4">
        <h1 class="fw-bold">Creating a Stored Procedure</h1>

        <p class="text-muted">
            Learn how to create a Stored Procedure in SQL Server using
            the CREATE PROCEDURE statement.
        </p>
    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         INTRODUCTION
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">Creating a Stored Procedure</h2>

            <p>
                A Stored Procedure is created using the
                <strong>CREATE PROCEDURE</strong> statement in SQL Server.
            </p>

            <p>
                A Stored Procedure can contain one or more SQL statements.
                Once created, it can be executed whenever required.
            </p>

            <p>
                Stored Procedures are useful for storing frequently used
                SQL operations inside the database.
            </p>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         BASIC SYNTAX
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">Basic Syntax</h2>

            <p>
                The basic syntax for creating a Stored Procedure is:
            </p>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>CREATE PROCEDURE ProcedureName
AS
BEGIN
    -- SQL statements
END;</code></pre>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         SIMPLE EXAMPLE
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">Simple Stored Procedure Example</h2>

            <p>
                Suppose we have a table named
                <strong>Students</strong>.
                We can create a Stored Procedure to display all students.
            </p>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>CREATE PROCEDURE GetAllStudents
AS
BEGIN

    SELECT *
    FROM Students;

END;</code></pre>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         EXECUTING PROCEDURE
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">Executing a Stored Procedure</h2>

            <p>
                After creating the Stored Procedure, we can execute it
                using the <strong>EXEC</strong> statement.
            </p>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>EXEC GetAllStudents;</code></pre>

            <p class="mt-3">
                The above statement executes the
                <strong>GetAllStudents</strong> Stored Procedure and
                returns the records from the Students table.
            </p>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         STORED PROCEDURE WITH WHERE
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Stored Procedure with WHERE Clause
            </h2>

            <p>
                A Stored Procedure can also contain conditions using
                the <strong>WHERE</strong> clause.
            </p>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>CREATE PROCEDURE GetActiveStudents
AS
BEGIN

    SELECT *
    FROM Students
    WHERE IsActive = 1;

END;</code></pre>

            <p class="mt-3">
                This procedure returns only the students whose
                <strong>IsActive</strong> value is 1.
            </p>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         CREATE OR ALTER
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">CREATE OR ALTER PROCEDURE</h2>

            <p>
                SQL Server also supports
                <strong>CREATE OR ALTER PROCEDURE</strong>.
                It can be used to create a new procedure or modify an
                existing procedure.
            </p>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>CREATE OR ALTER PROCEDURE GetAllStudents
AS
BEGIN

    SELECT *
    FROM Students;

END;</code></pre>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         IMPORTANT POINTS
    ========================== -->

    <div class="alert alert-warning mb-4">

        <h4 class="fw-bold">Important Points</h4>

        <ul class="mb-0">

            <li>
                Stored Procedures are created using
                <strong>CREATE PROCEDURE</strong>.
            </li>

            <li>
                SQL statements are written inside the procedure.
            </li>

            <li>
                <strong>EXEC</strong> is used to execute a Stored Procedure.
            </li>

            <li>
                A Stored Procedure can contain SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE
                and DELETE statements.
            </li>

            <li>
                Parameters can be added to make a Stored Procedure
                reusable.
            </li>

            <li>
                Stored Procedures can be modified using
                <strong>ALTER PROCEDURE</strong> or
                <strong>CREATE OR ALTER PROCEDURE</strong>.
            </li>

        </ul>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         ADVANTAGES
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Advantages of Stored Procedures
            </h2>

            <ul>

                <li>Reusable SQL code</li>

                <li>Improves database code organization</li>

                <li>Can accept input parameters</li>

                <li>Can return result sets</li>

                <li>Can contain multiple SQL statements</li>

                <li>Useful for implementing database operations</li>

            </ul>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         SUMMARY
    ========================== -->

    <div class="alert alert-info p-4 mb-4">

        <h2 class="fw-bold">Summary</h2>

        <p class="mb-0">
            A Stored Procedure is a pre-defined collection of SQL statements
            stored in the SQL Server database. It is created using
            <strong>CREATE PROCEDURE</strong> and executed using
            <strong>EXEC</strong>. Stored Procedures can contain different
            SQL operations and can also use parameters to make them more
            flexible and reusable.
        </p>

    </div>


